  "title": "Broadcast, depth and bypasses",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Broadcast, depth and bypasses (validated pipeline; exact on three small networks). (1) Broadcast: a hub (a 16-point grid or a cube) receiving a relay from a ring that carries an opened Fano handle, and emitting into two 16-point grids at the lines nearest its receiving point, relays the handle into both grids at once (5 ring points reach both through the 16-point grid, 2 through the cube); through strips after the hub no ring point reaches both. (2) Direction: in chains of strips, cubes, 16-point grids and thick tubes with the handle at every point, no creation ever lies upstream of the handle's piece. (3) Bypasses: stations whose two cut vertices are adjacent pass the relay without loss through 1 to 4 stations (5 ring points reach the final grid each time). (4) Exact: on a cube hub with two small prism receivers, an aligned chain three cuts deep and a two-cut relay (18 to 19 plane points), at the relaying ring points exact creation (join method) agrees with the pipeline in all 1,896 cases and creates in each receiver, three cuts away and two cuts away.",
